RISK MITIGATION AND KERNEL INTEGRITY\uc0\u8232 The Axion-Snooper requires Ring 0 (Kernel) access. The HASL layer reduces the risk profile from 4/10 to a stabilized 7/10 by enforcing V-Curve limits and Watchdog triggers. ISS ensures that even if the analog VRM is slow to react, the silicon gates remain within safe thermal boundaries, allowing for 24/7 high-intensity operation on commodity hardware.\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	10	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
CONCLUSION: THE FINAL FRONTIER OF PERFORMANCE\uc0\u8232 Axion Fabric v.1.0.0 proves that software-hardware co-design can compensate for physical hardware limitations. By treating the PC as a fluid electromagnetic system and controlling the instruction stream via ISS, we achieve "Mission-Critical" performance on standard silicon. The Fractal Snapshot, IMC-Snooping, and HASL Safety Layer represent the final bridge between the user\'92s intent and the raw computational power of the silicon.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
